                        Narrate(text: "Now there is a current. Electrons (blue) were already in all the metal. They all start to move at once, out of the negative terminal of the cell, round the loop and back into its positive terminal. So the lamp lights straight away.", for_s: 9.0, at_s: 3.0),
                        Narrate(text: "The current is the same everywhere in the loop: in every wire, through the switch, through the lamp's filament and through the cell. No charge is used up; it goes round and round.", for_s: 7.0, at_s: 12.0),
                        Narrate(text: "The cell gives the charge energy. In the thin filament that energy is transferred as heat and light. (Real electrons drift slowly, under a millimetre a second; here they are shown much faster.)", for_s: 6.0, at_s: 19.0),
